[gd_scene load_steps=8 format=3]

; ROCKET PODS — the Picket's launcher, as a model only.
;
; THE CHASSIS WAS SIZED TO THIS PACK AND THEN THE PACK WAS REMOVED.
; tools/build_picket.gd:196-205 keeps TUBE_R, TUBE_LEN, TUBE_COLS, TUBE_ROWS as
; constants precisely because the cradle is measured in them and nothing else:
; the mantlet is as wide as three tubes and as tall as two, the breech plane is
; where their rear faces were, and RAIL_LEN is a fraction of their length. So
; these numbers are not a style choice — they are the geometry the frame has a
; hole for. Six tubes, three across and two high, radius 0.14, length 1.375,
; spaced 0.322 (build_picket.gd:70-76).
;
; THE BORE RUNS ALONG +X. Every AI weapon in this project points down its own
; +X (ai_weapon_grenade_launcher.gd:246 says so in as many words) and
; picket.tscn:461 yaws the WeaponMount +PI/2 to turn that onto the assembly's
; -Z. A pack built along -Z here would fire sideways out of the cradle with
; nothing complaining.
;
; THE BORES ARE FAKED, NOT CUT. build_picket.gd's note describes CSGMesh3D
; tubes with a CSGCylinder3D subtraction each — correct for a one-off chassis
; bake, wrong for a weapon: a fitted weapon is instanced per robot per mission
; and six live CSG subtractions would be paid for every one of them. A dark
; inset disc at each muzzle face reads as an open tube at icon size and at
; gameplay distance, and costs one more MeshInstance3D.
;
; The pack starts at the origin and runs forward, so bolted to the WeaponMount
; at the breech plane it grows out of the cradle and overhangs the 0.78 m rails
; — which is the read build_picket.gd:242-246 intended. A pack that floats or
; that the rails pass through means the mount is wrong, not this.

